    "result_text": "I implemented `ask_with_audit` in `app/audit.py`, and it returns the request ID, the exact response body and the joined answer text.\n\n```python\ndef ask_with_audit(client: Anthropic, prompt: str) -> dict:\n    raw = client.messages.with_raw_response.create(\n        model=MODEL, max_tokens=256, messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}]\n    )\n    message = raw.parse()\n    return {\n        \"request_id\": raw.headers.get(\"request-id\"),\n        \"raw_body\": raw.text(),\n        \"answer\": \"\".join(block.text for block in message.content if block.type == \"text\"),\n    }\n```\n\n- **SDK check:** I read the installed anthropic 1.8.0 source first, because the raw-response code has moved since older versions. In this version, `with_raw_response` returns an `APIResponse` whose body is read in full, so calling both `.parse()` and `.text()` on it is safe.\n- **Missing header:** `request_id` is `None` if the response has no `request-id` header.\n- **Answer text:** it is joined the same way as `ask()` in `app/assistant.py`.\n\n**Testing:** `pytest -q` passes, but the only existing test just checks that `MODEL` starts with `claude-`. I also ran a script that sends a fake response containing two text blocks and a `request-id` header. It returned the header value, the exact body text and `\"Hello\"` as the answer. Nothing was sent to the real API.\n\n**Leftover file:** the script is `_check.py` in the project root. My attempt to delete it needed your approval and didn't go through, so please remove it yourself. It's also worth turning into a proper test in `tests/`, since nothing there covers `ask_with_audit` yet."
